    "result_text": "The full test suite is green \u2014 `AcceptanceTest` is the only test class in this project, and both of its tests pass along with a successful build.\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented the `locality` derivation on the Owner resource. Locality is a derived, read-only field computed purely from the owner's `city` via a fixed city-to-region table.\n\n**Changes:**\n\n1. **`src/main/resources/openapi.yml`** \u2014 Added a read-only `locality` string property to the `Owner` schema (the DTO is generated from this spec), so the field is serialized in `GET /api/owners/{id}` responses.\n\n2. **`src/main/java/.../mapper/OwnerMapper.java`** \u2014 Added:\n   - A fixed `CITY_REGION` table (`Sydney\u2192NSW`, `Melbourne\u2192VIC`, `Brisbane\u2192QLD`).\n   - A `@Mapping(target = \"locality\", expression = \"java(locality(owner))\")` on `toOwnerDto`.\n   - A `locality(Owner)` method returning the canonical region, or `\"UNKNOWN\"` when the city isn't in the table.\n\nThis follows the existing repository pattern where derived owner fields (`displayName`, `membershipTier`, `householdId`, etc.) are declared read-only in the OpenAPI spec and computed in the MapStruct mapper. Both acceptance tests pass: `coreDerivesRegionForKnownCity` (Sydney \u2192 NSW) and `functionalityUnknownCityIsUnknown` (random city \u2192 UNKNOWN).",
